+/// §16.9 (D30): the pocket with a SHELF, a flat face at Z 6.5 (between the
+/// floor and the top) on the +x side of the pocket. One level from the top
+/// to the floor drapes the cut up onto the shelf. The shelf's stock above
+/// its leave stands up to the top (Z 10), so where the cut climbs onto the
+/// shelf the tool's disc meets a band of stock spanning the whole disc: a
+/// step within one pass deep (3 mm against Depth/Pass 6) but wider than
+/// c·D. The width read must split such steps (`width_split > 0` over the
+/// arms), and per arm the simulation must read no more MOVES over the
+/// exact bound than the same plan under the historical path-shape split
